    <briefdescription>
<para>Retrieve layout associated with a domain decomposition. Given a global 2D domain and the number of divisions in the decomposition ndivs (usually the PE count unless some domains are <emphasis>masked</emphasis>) this calls returns a 2D domain layout. By default, <ref refid="interfacempp__domains__mod_1_1mpp__define__layout" kindref="compound">mpp_define_layout</ref> will attempt to divide the 2D index space into domains that maintain the aspect ratio of the global domain. If this cannot be done, the algorithm favours domains that are longer in <emphasis>x</emphasis> than <emphasis>y</emphasis>, a preference that could improve vector performance. <linebreak/>
Example usage: </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><programlisting filename=".F90"><codeline><highlight class="keyword">call<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="interfacempp__domains__mod_1_1mpp__define__layout" kindref="compound">mpp_define_layout</ref>(<sp/>global_indices,<sp/>ndivs,<sp/>layout<sp/>)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>    </detaileddescription>
